# __SERVER_NAME__

Generated from the canonical `ai-skills` .NET MCP server template. It is an architecture seed with domain code isolated from MCP, fail-closed manifests, one invocation kernel, and conservative local transport defaults.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This generated project is not production-accepted by generation alone. Replace the in-memory adapter, review the public capability contract, and complete the applicable identity, authorization, CI/CD, deployment-artifact, and adoption work before production use.

## Quick start

Restore and build the generated server and its smoke project with the committed lock files:

```bash
dotnet restore tests/__NAMESPACE__.Mcp.Smoke/__NAMESPACE__.Mcp.Smoke.csproj --locked-mode
dotnet build tests/__NAMESPACE__.Mcp.Smoke/__NAMESPACE__.Mcp.Smoke.csproj -c Release --no-restore
```

Stdio is the default transport. For loopback Streamable HTTP, pass `--http` and set `MCP_HTTP_BEARER_TOKEN` to at least 32 random characters. Legacy `/sse` and `/message` endpoints are intentionally absent. Modern Streamable HTTP may still use `text/event-stream` framing; that is not the deprecated two-endpoint transport.

## Capabilities

The generated server's application-owned canonical capability manifest is the static source of truth, while runtime MCP discovery is the authoritative active view. Keep README content at capability-group and representative-workflow level rather than maintaining a second exact tool catalog.

## Security

- Stdio is the default and does not expose an MCP network listener.
- Streamable HTTP is restricted to loopback and requires a development bearer token.
- Every transport reaches the same application-owned invocation kernel rather than implementing policy independently.
- Mutation behavior remains subject to the generated operation gate and manifest policy.
- Remote/public HTTP is not part of the generated production-ready profile; replace development identity and authorization before extending the deployment boundary.

